== Notes ==
* In their tablet form, they appear to be immobile and will activate [[Reform Carvings]] immediately after being [[aggro]]ed; this causes them to revert to the tablet form before assuming a new form.
** Their most common form is as a Mesmer; they also use this whenever they are alone when attacked.
*** Their Mesmer form resembles a [[naga]].
** They turn into Dervishes when they are low on health.
*** Their Dervish form resembles [[drake]]s.
** They sometimes turn into Paragons when they are within earshot of their allies.
*** Their Paragon form resembles [[kraken]]s.

{{bug|When knocked down in tablet form, Graven Monoliths sometimes get stuck and stop performing any actions.}}

== Trivia ==
* Their dying animation will be one of the forms they had before first using [[Reform Carvings]].
* On occasion you may see a graven monolith wielding an [[Aureate Aegis]].
* The Graven Monolith is one of very few types of [[NPC]]s that can use skills from three different [[profession]]s.
